prose:
Tut, our Horses they shall not see, I'le tye them in the wood;
our Vizards we will change after we leave them: and, Sarrah, I have
Cases of Buckram for the nonce, to immask our noted outward Garments.

Come my Masters, let us share, and then to Horse before day;
and the Prince and Poynes be not two arrand Cowards, there's no equity
stirring. There's no more Valour in that Poynes, than in a wild Duck.

Ye lye, Hostess: Bardolph was shav'd, and lost many a Hair;
and I'll be sworn my Pocket was pick'd; go to, you are a Woman,
go.
